WEBVTT

00:02.369 --> 00:05.601
<i>[Singing] It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.706 --> 00:08.800
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.910 --> 00:12.641
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.748 --> 00:15.479
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.985 --> 00:18.819
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.323 --> 00:22.350
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:22.460 --> 00:24.155
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.262 --> 00:25.923
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:26.031 --> 00:30.834
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.209 --> 00:37.734
Peter, this game night was a great idea.

00:37.845 --> 00:40.041
Yeah, this will be a lot more fun
than last Saturday...

00:40.149 --> 00:41.741
<i>when we went to see
The Vagina Monologues.</i>

00:41.850 --> 00:45.981
So, in international news,
no luck yet finding Osama bin Laden.

00:46.089 --> 00:49.992
So the government is trying a new tactic.
They've hired Jeff Gillooly.

00:50.094 --> 00:51.083
[Audience member coughing]

00:51.195 --> 00:52.458
Gillooly.

00:52.731 --> 00:53.720
[Man clearing throat]

00:53.832 --> 00:58.600
Sorry, I guess that joke was not so fresh,
but you know...

01:01.275 --> 01:03.106
Okay, Joe. Right foot, green.

01:03.210 --> 01:05.270
All right, let's do it!

01:05.480 --> 01:07.812
Yes! I am the king!

01:07.949 --> 01:10.919
Thanks for including
my civil rights board game...

01:11.020 --> 01:13.250
in the game night rotation, guys.

01:13.355 --> 01:16.416
We're always happy to play
Two Decades of Dignity.

01:16.526 --> 01:19.052
It makes us all feel a little less guilty.

01:22.033 --> 01:24.025
For whistling at a white woman,
go directly to jail.

01:24.136 --> 01:26.263
Man, does anyone ever win at this game?

01:26.371 --> 01:30.069
You don't win.
You just do a little better each time.

01:30.944 --> 01:33.539
Okay, everybody, time for paintball.

01:33.647 --> 01:35.343
I forgot to pick up the paintball guns.

01:35.450 --> 01:38.886
Well, we could use these.
I brought them from the office.

01:39.588 --> 01:42.524
Peter, is it safe to be firing real guns
at each other in the house?

01:42.625 --> 01:45.823
All right, all right, nobody fire at Lois.
She's scared.

01:46.230 --> 01:47.993
All right, one, two, three, go!

01:49.267 --> 01:50.700
[Guns firing]

01:52.671 --> 01:53.933
[AII exclaiming]

01:59.880 --> 02:01.245
Missed, you ass.

02:02.416 --> 02:04.577
- Damn it, Peter, that hurt.
- Relax, Quagmire.

02:04.685 --> 02:07.746
<i>You're doing better than Peter Weller
from the opening scene of RoboCop.</i>

02:10.793 --> 02:14.058
Well, now that the mess is cleaned up and
we're back from the emergency room...

02:14.164 --> 02:16.827
it's time for the last game of the night,
Trivial Pursuit.

02:16.934 --> 02:20.530
Man, I hate Trivial Pursuit.
Always makes me feel so stupid.

02:20.639 --> 02:23.302
More stupid than that time
you locked your keys out of the car?

02:23.709 --> 02:24.676
Damn it!

02:24.977 --> 02:28.379
Hey! Hey! Somebody! Hey!

02:28.549 --> 02:31.542
Hey, sir! Sir, you see those keys there? Sir!

02:31.753 --> 02:33.050
Oh, screw you!

02:42.799 --> 02:44.289
All right, Brian, this one's for you.

02:44.401 --> 02:48.965
"What naturally occurring element has
the highest melting point of all metals?"

02:49.274 --> 02:51.367
- Cadmium?
- Sorry, tungsten.

02:51.677 --> 02:52.939
Dumb ass. My turn. What do you got?

02:53.045 --> 02:56.482
Okay, here we go.
"What color is a fire truck?"

02:56.983 --> 02:58.747
Oh, God, I always get these.

02:58.919 --> 03:00.978
Okay, all right, fire truck.

03:01.155 --> 03:05.650
Fire truck, fire truck, fire truck, fire truck,
what color are those red fire trucks?

03:06.094 --> 03:08.586
Oh, God, I can picture them now,
all red and everything.

03:08.698 --> 03:10.997
That's right, Peter, they are red.

03:11.101 --> 03:12.295
Lois, what are you doing?

03:12.402 --> 03:15.031
[Whispering] I switched Peter's questions
to the pre-school edition.

03:15.139 --> 03:16.606
Just to let him have his moment.

03:16.708 --> 03:20.509
Good thing I just watched that
National Geographic special on fire trucks.

03:20.679 --> 03:24.241
<i>NARRATOR: A solitary killer,
the fire truck stalks its prey.</i>

03:40.904 --> 03:44.396
<i>The fire truck can consume
eight times its body weight.</i>

03:46.111 --> 03:47.942
[Horn blaring]

03:48.046 --> 03:50.379
<i>NARRATOR: The ambulances
will have to wait their turn.</i>

03:50.783 --> 03:54.720
Okay, Brian, "Name the 16th century
ecumenical body...

03:54.821 --> 03:57.813
"that marked a major turning point
for Christianity in Europe."

03:57.924 --> 04:00.155
I think that was the Council of Trent.

04:01.029 --> 04:03.294
You could not be more wrong.

04:03.532 --> 04:05.261
The answer is Phyllis Diller.

04:05.367 --> 04:07.495
- Peter, you're reading the pink...
- My turn.

04:07.604 --> 04:09.595
Okay, Peter, this is for the win.

04:09.706 --> 04:12.005
"Say the word 'what."'

04:14.445 --> 04:15.811
Wow. Okay.

04:17.316 --> 04:19.911
This really separates the men
from the boys.

04:23.890 --> 04:25.188
Peter, just say "what."

04:25.292 --> 04:29.229
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, now, Lois.
This is not a race.

04:29.998 --> 04:32.193
Okay, I wanna say "who."

04:33.869 --> 04:35.063
Oh, boy.

04:35.404 --> 04:36.871
<i>Fantastic Four.</i>

04:37.441 --> 04:42.379
<i>Fantastic Four, steak, steak, steak, steak,
a small amount of peas.</i>

04:43.548 --> 04:44.537
Is it "what?"

04:44.649 --> 04:47.619
That's right. You win, Peter. You did it.

04:47.720 --> 04:49.985
Oh, my God! I won. I won!

04:50.090 --> 04:51.648
My dad's smarter than your dad.

04:51.758 --> 04:55.627
- We have the same dad, idiot.
- Yeah, but mine's smarter.

04:55.730 --> 04:56.958
What a feeling.

04:57.064 --> 04:59.932
This is even better than that time
I met Timer the Cheese Guy.

05:00.035 --> 05:03.062
<i>[Singing] I hanker for a hunk of
A slab or slice or chunk of</i>

05:03.172 --> 05:05.367
<i>I hanker for a hunk of cheese</i>

05:05.475 --> 05:08.775
<i>When your get-up-and-go
has got up and went</i>

05:09.680 --> 05:10.772
Howdy, pardner.

05:10.881 --> 05:12.747
Pardon me, sir. I live next door.

05:12.884 --> 05:16.184
It is 3:30 in the morning. I am very tired.

05:16.288 --> 05:17.778
Look, a wagon wheel.

05:17.890 --> 05:19.084
What the hell is your problem?

05:19.191 --> 05:20.853
I just smoked a whole bunch of crack.

05:21.395 --> 05:22.726
Good night, losers.

05:23.463 --> 05:25.159
Well, game night was a success.

05:25.266 --> 05:28.133
Peter, you do know that all your questions
were incredibly easy.

05:28.236 --> 05:30.865
Yeah, easy for me. Good night, morons.

05:31.440 --> 05:34.035
You ever stop and think,
"Wow, I'm married to that guy"?

05:34.144 --> 05:35.577
No, I just repress it.

05:35.678 --> 05:38.512
- Is that healthy?
- What's the worst that could happen?

05:38.716 --> 05:40.183
<i>[Singing] I'm a tumor, I'm a tumor</i>

05:40.284 --> 05:42.515
<i>I'm a tumor, I'm a tumor, I'm a tumor</i>

05:42.621 --> 05:44.680
<i>I'm a tumor, I'm a tumor, I'm a tumor</i>

05:44.856 --> 05:46.381
<i>Oh, oh, oh, I'm a tumor</i>

05:48.594 --> 05:52.258
<i>The administration's plan for peace
in the Middle East is shallow and pedantic.</i>

05:52.366 --> 05:55.200
<i>I agree. Shallow and pedantic.</i>

05:55.570 --> 05:58.164
I agree as well. Shallow and pedantic.

06:01.076 --> 06:02.441
Everything all right. Peter?

06:02.545 --> 06:06.004
Well, Lois, since you asked, I find
this meatloaf rather shallow and pedantic.

06:06.116 --> 06:08.108
What is this,
you're gonna talk down to everyone...

06:08.219 --> 06:10.153
just because you won a game
of Trivial Pursuit?

06:10.254 --> 06:11.221
Perhaps.

06:11.322 --> 06:13.518
Okay, you know what?
Fine, you are a genius, Peter.

06:13.625 --> 06:15.149
As a matter of fact, let's make it official.

06:15.260 --> 06:17.320
You ever heard
of the MacArthur genius grant?

06:17.430 --> 06:18.397
Perhaps.

06:18.498 --> 06:20.125
Well, if you qualify as a genius...

06:20.233 --> 06:22.668
the Foundation will give you
a $500,000 grant...

06:22.770 --> 06:24.362
just to sit around
and do whatever you want.

06:24.472 --> 06:28.239
Wow! Imagine what a genius like me
could do with all that money.

06:28.443 --> 06:30.912
All right, Cloris Leachman,
I've bought you legally.

06:31.013 --> 06:32.275
Now juggle these beanbags.

06:32.381 --> 06:33.643
I don't know how to juggle...

06:33.750 --> 06:35.342
God help you, Cloris!
Juggle the beanbags!

06:39.157 --> 06:41.648
You may begin your exam now.

06:47.267 --> 06:48.894
<i>MALE VOICE: A dog says...</i>

06:49.002 --> 06:49.969
[Dog barking]

06:51.439 --> 06:52.997
<i>A cow says...</i>

06:53.441 --> 06:54.669
[Cow mooing]

06:55.410 --> 06:56.741
Of course, of course.

06:58.313 --> 07:01.613
Well, here they are, Brian. My test results.
Read them and weep.

07:02.085 --> 07:04.145
Peter, according to this,
you're not a genius.

07:04.255 --> 07:06.246
In fact, you're mentally retarded.

07:06.357 --> 07:06.524
Oh, yeah?
Well, would a mentally retarded guy...

07:06.524 --> 07:09.050
Oh, yeah?
Well, would a mentally retarded guy...

07:09.160 --> 07:12.186
have hired a bulldozer with a drunk driver
to level half of his house...

07:12.297 --> 07:14.562
in celebration of his fantastic test results?

07:15.101 --> 07:16.068
Maybe.

07:16.235 --> 07:17.203
Uh-oh.

07:18.639 --> 07:20.766
Congratulations.

07:25.714 --> 07:29.047
So, as you can see, you are just
over the line of mental retardation.

07:29.151 --> 07:30.551
Don't you mean, just under the line?

07:30.654 --> 07:32.554
The day I'm corrected by a...

07:32.856 --> 07:36.452
I'm sorry. Just please trust the analysis.

07:38.062 --> 07:39.291
Hello. Sally?

07:39.398 --> 07:40.888
Hey, it's Peter Griffin.

07:40.999 --> 07:44.401
That's right, senior prom.
Yeah. Yeah, it's been a while, yeah.

07:44.604 --> 07:46.469
So, listen.

07:46.739 --> 07:48.503
I just found out I'm retarded.

07:48.609 --> 07:51.773
And I'm just calling to let you know...

07:52.747 --> 07:54.942
you might want to get yourself tested.

07:56.552 --> 07:57.644
Hello?

07:57.954 --> 08:00.788
Peter, mental retardation usually happens
before you're born.

08:00.891 --> 08:03.951
It isn't something you can catch.
Don't you think you're overreacting?

08:04.061 --> 08:06.394
Well, excuse me for being retarded.

08:06.497 --> 08:08.522
My whole world
has been turned upside down.

08:08.633 --> 08:10.124
Black is east, up is white.

08:10.235 --> 08:14.366
You know, Peter, I hate to say "I told you
so" about not being a genius, but...

08:14.474 --> 08:18.377
yeah! In your... face,!

08:20.948 --> 08:22.109
I'm sorry about that.

08:22.217 --> 08:25.846
I can't believe this is happening to me.
I can never go back to school again.

08:25.954 --> 08:27.354
Oh, yes, Meg, yes.

08:27.457 --> 08:29.755
Yes, everything was going
swimmingly for you until this.

08:29.859 --> 08:32.727
Yes, this is the thing
that will ruin your reputation.

08:32.830 --> 08:36.358
Not your years of grotesque appearance
or awkward social graces...

08:36.468 --> 08:39.165
or that Felix Unger-ish way
you clear your sinuses.

08:39.271 --> 08:40.568
No, no, no, it's this.

08:40.673 --> 08:43.301
Do you hear yourself talk?
I might kill you tonight.

08:43.510 --> 08:45.478
Peter, you're still you.

08:45.579 --> 08:47.570
No piece of paper from the city
is gonna tell me...

08:47.681 --> 08:49.912
you're any different
from the man I married.

08:50.018 --> 08:51.781
And your life's not gonna change
because of it.

08:51.886 --> 08:52.876
[Clanking]

08:52.988 --> 08:53.955
What is that?

08:56.191 --> 08:57.921
Oh, my God, what are they doing?

08:58.028 --> 09:00.896
Why are they trying
to publicly humiliate me like this?

09:00.998 --> 09:03.660
I mean, what's the purpose...
Shiny red ball.

09:04.535 --> 09:06.094
Peter, watch out!

09:09.274 --> 09:10.537
So what can I do for you, Peter?

09:10.643 --> 09:13.510
Well, Joe, I need to talk to you
about something kind of personal.

09:13.613 --> 09:15.479
- Shoot.
- Well, you know, I took this test...

09:15.582 --> 09:20.043
and it sort of turns out
that I'm technically mentally retarded.

09:20.321 --> 09:23.018
And, you know, I just wanted to ask...

09:23.192 --> 09:25.160
you know, how do you deal with it?

09:25.294 --> 09:27.889
- Deal with what?
- You know, with being retarded.

09:27.998 --> 09:30.364
Peter, I'm not retarded. I'm handicapped.

09:30.467 --> 09:31.935
Now you're just splitting hairs.

09:34.372 --> 09:36.068
<i>[Singing] Hi, Cleveland</i>

09:36.175 --> 09:37.665
<i>Hi, Joseph</i>

09:37.776 --> 09:41.577
<i>What's the story, morning glory?
What's the word, hummingbird?</i>

09:41.681 --> 09:43.672
<i>Have you heard?
Peter Griffin is slow</i>

09:43.783 --> 09:47.049
<i>Can he still drive a car?
Can he drink at a bar?</i>

09:47.188 --> 09:50.420
<i>Will they let him have kids?
Is his life on the skids?</i>

09:50.525 --> 09:53.962
<i>Hello, Mrs. Griffin,
it's your neighbor, Quagmire</i>

09:54.063 --> 09:57.761
<i>Now that Peter's mental
You probably have some needs</i>

09:58.235 --> 10:01.569
<i>He's retarded
Peter is</i>

10:01.673 --> 10:04.938
<i>He's retarded
Peter is</i>

10:05.043 --> 10:09.674
<i>He's retarded
Peter is slow</i>

10:12.519 --> 10:13.884
Griffin. Party of two.

10:13.987 --> 10:16.218
Mr. Griffin, we've been expecting you.

10:16.324 --> 10:19.123
Peter, relax. It's for liability reasons.

10:19.228 --> 10:21.059
Now, let's just try to enjoy our meal.

10:21.163 --> 10:23.394
I kind of get the helmet.
But what's with the water wings?

10:23.500 --> 10:24.831
Well, you did order the soup.

10:24.934 --> 10:26.959
Like something could happen...

10:27.070 --> 10:30.973
Get me out!

10:32.711 --> 10:34.975
These water wings didn't help at all.

10:35.982 --> 10:37.813
This is the worst day of my life.

10:37.917 --> 10:40.512
Now, there are plenty of people
who have had worse days.

10:43.991 --> 10:46.790
A parking ticket. I was gone five minutes.

10:47.962 --> 10:50.124
How could this day get any worse?

10:51.967 --> 10:54.198
Oh, my God.

10:56.706 --> 10:57.799
Oh, no!

10:59.877 --> 11:02.972
I wish I could just close my eyes
and make all this go away.

11:03.081 --> 11:04.673
Peter, look out!

11:05.250 --> 11:06.343
Holy crap!

11:07.120 --> 11:08.144
Oh, my God!

11:08.254 --> 11:09.585
Mr. Tucker, are you all right?

11:09.689 --> 11:12.989
Do I look like I'm all right?
My back is broken and my leg is twisted!

11:13.093 --> 11:15.324
Oh, my God! Your hooker's dead.

11:15.430 --> 11:17.762
Well, she was already dead,
but that doesn't excuse...

11:17.866 --> 11:20.131
Wait a minute.
You're Peter Griffin, the retarded fellow.

11:20.236 --> 11:22.227
- Yeah.
- Well, then don't worry about it.

11:22.338 --> 11:24.830
Wait a minute. You mean
you're not even gonna call the cops?

11:24.942 --> 11:28.174
Oh, my God.
I could get away with anything.

11:29.581 --> 11:32.244
"And on the sixth day, God said:

11:32.351 --> 11:35.252
"'Let the Earth bring forth
the living creatures and..."'

11:35.354 --> 11:36.754
Bible fight!

11:39.726 --> 11:40.716
[Woman 1 screaming]

11:40.828 --> 11:42.955
- Sorry. Retarded.
- That's okay then.

11:43.130 --> 11:44.119
[Woman 2 screaming]

11:44.232 --> 11:46.701
- Don't know any better.
- Bless your heart.

11:46.935 --> 11:48.061
[Woman 3 screaming]

11:48.170 --> 11:50.264
Jeez, didn't you hear me a second ago?
I'm retarded.

11:51.074 --> 11:52.507
You're just curious.

11:52.642 --> 11:55.168
Well, let me show you
how everything works down there.

11:58.183 --> 11:59.150
Hey, everyone.

11:59.251 --> 12:02.688
Say hello to my state-appointed
inspirational social worker, Vern.

12:02.788 --> 12:04.187
It's truly a pleasure to meet you all.

12:04.290 --> 12:07.692
Hey, Peter, looks like you've got yourself
one super family.

12:07.794 --> 12:10.262
High five! All right!

12:12.200 --> 12:15.364
So, Vern, what exactly is it that you do?

12:15.471 --> 12:18.167
I'm here to lend a hand
to my main man, Peter.

12:18.274 --> 12:19.536
- Right, Peter?
- Right.

12:19.643 --> 12:22.009
High five! All right!

12:23.146 --> 12:24.114
Done.

12:24.815 --> 12:26.646
- Peter!
- What? I don't know any better.

12:26.751 --> 12:28.413
Peter, I don't like this.

12:28.520 --> 12:31.284
You are really starting to take advantage
of this whole situation.

12:31.390 --> 12:33.154
Peter's just expressing himself.

12:33.259 --> 12:35.193
High five for expressing yourself, Peter.

12:35.295 --> 12:37.093
High five! All right!

12:39.566 --> 12:43.003
This man seems bent on diluting
the already watered-down significance...

12:43.104 --> 12:44.435
of the elevated hand slap.

12:44.539 --> 12:46.508
- Hey, Stewie, high five.
- Well, it's about time.

12:46.609 --> 12:47.701
- Psych.
- Damn!

12:47.810 --> 12:50.507
I look even more foolish
than when I was at that cocktail party.

12:50.747 --> 12:53.841
All right, you're gonna love this. So...
Hang on a sec.

13:07.601 --> 13:10.729
Okay, so these two black guys
walk into a bar, and the bartender looks...

13:10.838 --> 13:12.101
Hey, what are you guys talking about?

13:12.207 --> 13:14.232
I was just telling a joke.

13:14.876 --> 13:17.641
So, the bartender looks around and says:

13:17.747 --> 13:20.011
"What'll you two fine gentlemen have?"

13:20.284 --> 13:24.654
And they paid their tab
and couldn't have been more courteous.

13:26.257 --> 13:29.716
All right, my first trip to a fast-food joint
as a retarded guy.

13:29.829 --> 13:32.127
Excuse me, pardon me, coming through.
Special needs.

13:32.231 --> 13:34.792
Yeah, I'll have a... Is this thing on?

13:35.502 --> 13:39.769
<i>Attention, restaurant customers.
Testicles. That is all.</i>

13:39.874 --> 13:41.034
Give me that.

13:41.142 --> 13:45.341
<i>Sorry, folks. Oh, my God.
Is that what my voice sounds like?</i>

13:45.547 --> 13:48.312
<i>It's all whiney and nasally.</i>

13:48.418 --> 13:50.215
You know what?
I'm just gonna get my own food.

13:50.320 --> 13:53.290
- Peter, get back here.
- No freaking way.

13:53.457 --> 13:56.621
The fryolator. I am so taking this.

13:58.397 --> 13:59.558
[Lois screaming]

14:00.733 --> 14:03.669
<i>Lois, you look worse than
that Rocky Dennis kid from Mask.</i>

14:03.771 --> 14:06.103
Rocky, I don't even know
what you look like.

14:06.473 --> 14:09.204
- Can I touch your face?
- Of course, Diana.

14:09.811 --> 14:10.937
Oh, God.

14:11.579 --> 14:13.946
Oh, God. What is this?

14:15.251 --> 14:16.776
What is all this?

14:16.953 --> 14:19.319
Am I touching the outside of a house?

14:19.489 --> 14:22.288
Oh, God! You're a monster.

14:22.393 --> 14:24.020
I'm beautiful on the inside.

14:24.128 --> 14:26.222
Yeah, but, Rocky, there's a limit.

14:27.633 --> 14:31.126
What is this now?
Does your face have a pelvis?

14:32.939 --> 14:36.000
Oh, God, what have I done?
I'm the worst husband ever.

14:36.110 --> 14:37.839
Make that the worst father ever.

14:37.946 --> 14:41.109
Hi, I'm Agent Jessup from Child Services.
I'm here to take your kids away.

14:41.216 --> 14:42.275
What? Why?

14:42.385 --> 14:44.785
Because you're mentally unfit
to take care of them.

14:44.887 --> 14:45.854
No way!

14:45.955 --> 14:47.082
- Oh, my God.
- Finally.

14:50.727 --> 14:52.753
I can't believe they took the kids away.

14:52.864 --> 14:55.100
Well, at least Cleveland offered
to take care of them.

14:56.635 --> 15:01.198
Sorry you have to share a bed, boys.
I'm a little short on space.

15:01.308 --> 15:02.798
Have a good sleep.

15:04.011 --> 15:05.239
Hey, Chris...

15:05.580 --> 15:07.514
whatever happened to Geena Davis?

15:07.782 --> 15:11.082
She used to be in movies,
but she's not in movies anymore.

15:11.220 --> 15:12.552
She's attractive enough...

15:12.655 --> 15:15.146
but when she smiles,
you see too much gum.

15:15.358 --> 15:17.589
Not a good tooth-to-gum ratio.

15:18.496 --> 15:19.588
Chris?

15:20.264 --> 15:22.062
I'll tell you tomorrow.

15:23.101 --> 15:25.399
Thanks for letting my friends sleep over,
Mr. Brown.

15:25.505 --> 15:26.631
No problem, Meg.

15:26.739 --> 15:30.232
If y'all get hungry,
there's some cottage cheese in the fridge.

15:30.377 --> 15:33.972
I'm gonna get me a spoonful now
before y'all have at it.

15:34.081 --> 15:36.846
Oh, my God.
Craig Hoffman's new car is so cool.

15:36.951 --> 15:39.011
Oh, my God. Totally. I love the color.

15:39.121 --> 15:40.611
Really? What color is it?

15:40.723 --> 15:42.520
It's like blue, kind of blue-green.

15:42.959 --> 15:44.824
It's the same color as his eyes.

15:44.928 --> 15:47.864
Wow. I bet he looks so hot driving it.

15:47.965 --> 15:49.398
I heard he bought it from his dad.

15:49.500 --> 15:51.867
Yeah, I remember his dad
dropped him off at school in it...

15:51.970 --> 15:53.460
one time when he was a freshman.

15:53.572 --> 15:55.631
- Doesn't his dad live in Hartford?
- I think so.

15:55.742 --> 15:57.266
My aunt Sheila lives in Hartford.

15:57.377 --> 16:00.142
They have a mall there that's pretty cool.
It's part underground.

16:00.247 --> 16:01.578
That's awesome.

16:01.682 --> 16:03.650
Damn it, you guys are boring
the crap out of me.

16:03.751 --> 16:05.617
It's stupid, mindless chatter, is what it is.

16:05.720 --> 16:06.744
You know what I'm gonna do?

16:06.855 --> 16:09.381
I'm just gonna go back to my place
and rent a dirty movie.

16:09.492 --> 16:11.187
This is ridiculous.

16:11.360 --> 16:14.922
That was weird. Oh, well.
Hey, let's compare breasts.

16:17.435 --> 16:19.528
Lois? Hey, how you doing, honey?

16:19.671 --> 16:21.765
Listen, there's no toilet paper
in the bathroom...

16:21.874 --> 16:23.364
so, I'm just gonna...

16:24.043 --> 16:25.010
There we go.

16:26.913 --> 16:28.210
[Toilet flushing]

16:28.315 --> 16:30.944
Oh, God. Hang on!

16:31.052 --> 16:34.180
The doctors still don't know how
much longer she's gonna have to be here.

16:34.288 --> 16:35.551
I feel horrible, Brian.

16:35.657 --> 16:38.285
I put Lois in the hospital, and I lost the
kids.

16:38.393 --> 16:41.158
This is turning out worse
than Stewie's iPod commercial.

16:52.712 --> 16:55.044
Peter, you just need to show
what a good father you are.

16:55.147 --> 16:56.945
Then you can get
the kids back from Cleveland.

16:57.050 --> 16:58.881
Wait a second, Brian. You're right.

16:58.986 --> 17:02.616
And the best way to do that is to show
what a terrible father Cleveland is.

17:02.724 --> 17:05.717
This plan is so perfect, it's retarded.

17:09.031 --> 17:10.590
<i>Good evening. I'm Dan Rather.</i>

17:10.700 --> 17:13.134
<i>And tonight on CBS News...</i>

17:13.236 --> 17:15.671
<i>seven Saudi soldiers sodomize...</i>

17:15.773 --> 17:20.006
<i>several of Saddam 's
southern settlement squatters.</i>

17:20.712 --> 17:22.305
[Whistling]

17:27.888 --> 17:28.980
<i>I'm Dan Rather.</i>

17:29.423 --> 17:31.517
All right, come on, ladies. Right this way.

17:31.626 --> 17:33.992
This'll show them
that Cleveland's not fit to be a parent.

17:34.095 --> 17:37.122
So, tell me, is there any tread left
on the tires at all?

17:37.233 --> 17:40.499
Or at this point, would it be like
throwing a hot dog down a hallway?

17:40.604 --> 17:42.469
Oh, my Lord. Look who's here.

17:42.572 --> 17:45.269
Agent Jessup,
look at all these prostitutes.

17:45.376 --> 17:48.471
<i>[Singing] One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven</i>

17:48.714 --> 17:50.909
Seven. Seven prostitutes.

17:51.016 --> 17:52.507
This is a shakedown.

17:52.619 --> 17:54.348
Mr. Griffin, this isn't going to work.

17:54.454 --> 17:57.822
Yeah. Peter, you and five
of those prostitutes, get out.

18:00.061 --> 18:03.828
So, in conclusion, Peter Griffin,
you've inspired me...

18:04.099 --> 18:06.364
to distrust
all mentally challenged parents.

18:06.469 --> 18:07.458
Thank you, Your Honor.

18:07.570 --> 18:10.972
And thank you, Agent Jessup,
for your comically misleading remarks.

18:11.075 --> 18:14.067
Mr. Griffin, do you have anything to say
in your defense...

18:14.179 --> 18:17.239
as to why this court should return custody
of your children to you?

18:17.349 --> 18:20.319
Your Honor, I would like to call
to the stand my surprise witness...

18:20.419 --> 18:22.387
The Ghost That Never Lies.

18:22.621 --> 18:24.180
[Exclaiming in surprise]

18:24.291 --> 18:26.259
But I'm the only one
who can see him and hear him...

18:26.360 --> 18:28.386
so I'll let everyone know
what he's saying and doing.

18:28.496 --> 18:30.623
Objection, Your Honor. This is ridiculous.

18:30.732 --> 18:32.428
Overruled. I'll allow it.

18:32.534 --> 18:35.025
You better be going somewhere
with this, Mr. Griffin.

18:35.137 --> 18:36.400
Thank you, Your Honor.

18:36.506 --> 18:38.133
Ghost That Never Lies...

18:38.241 --> 18:41.541
did you witness the events
that took place on that fateful day?

18:41.912 --> 18:44.210
You did? Well, how interesting.

18:44.449 --> 18:48.249
And, do you see the culprit or culprits
in this courtroom today?

18:48.520 --> 18:49.681
You do?

18:50.089 --> 18:53.787
Well, would you kindly
point him or them out for this court?

18:54.194 --> 18:56.025
Don't point at me, you jackass!

18:56.130 --> 18:58.861
Well, if there's nothing further,
I hereby sentence...

18:58.967 --> 19:01.561
Wait, wait, wait.
Your Honor, there is something further.

19:01.670 --> 19:03.865
Look, I know I screwed up big time.

19:03.973 --> 19:06.238
But I only did it
so I could get my kids back.

19:06.343 --> 19:07.310
I love them.

19:07.411 --> 19:09.845
And I think it's a bum rap
that just because I'm retarded...

19:09.946 --> 19:11.414
that makes me an unfit parent.

19:11.516 --> 19:14.314
There are plenty of unfit parents out there
who aren't retarded...

19:14.419 --> 19:15.546
but they get to keep their kids.

19:15.654 --> 19:19.421
Bing Crosby, Joan Crawford.
I think the Ramseys still got one left.

19:19.526 --> 19:22.689
I just want them back, Your Honor,
and you're the only one who can help me.

19:22.796 --> 19:23.786
What do you say?

19:23.898 --> 19:25.832
Are you kidding? You're a monster.

19:25.933 --> 19:27.697
In fact, if I could...

19:27.936 --> 19:31.736
I would put you in a place where you
would be removed from the general public.

19:31.840 --> 19:35.174
Perhaps locked in a big, secure building
with other dangerous people...

19:35.278 --> 19:37.179
for a pre-determined period of time...

19:37.281 --> 19:39.579
based on the nature and degree
of your offense.

19:39.683 --> 19:42.619
Unfortunately, as far as I know,
no such place exists.

19:42.720 --> 19:45.349
So I have no choice but to set you free.

19:45.458 --> 19:46.823
Does that mean I get my kids back?

19:46.926 --> 19:48.860
Absolutely not. Case closed.

19:48.961 --> 19:49.986
Oh, crap!

19:50.430 --> 19:52.557
It was prison you were thinking of. Prison.

19:52.666 --> 19:54.259
I already banged the hammer.

19:56.804 --> 19:58.830
<i>MAN: [On TV] And now,
back to Jake and the Fatman.</i>

19:58.941 --> 20:01.967
Hey, look over here on the carpet.
That's a cigarette butt.

20:02.077 --> 20:04.069
This is probably evidence.

20:06.750 --> 20:09.685
What do you think was in that Danish?

20:10.321 --> 20:12.756
You think it was cheese?

20:13.992 --> 20:16.621
'Cause I got a little problem with cheese.

20:16.729 --> 20:19.631
Hey, I'm talking about evidence here.
There's lipstick on it.

20:19.733 --> 20:22.827
Yeah, well, can you bring it over to me?

20:22.936 --> 20:25.337
I can't move it. This is a crime scene.

20:27.208 --> 20:29.177
Well, can you describe it to me?

20:29.378 --> 20:31.505
You know what? Forget it.
I'll take care of this, okay?

20:31.614 --> 20:34.948
Oh, no. Just...

20:38.489 --> 20:40.150
Just let me close my eyes for a minute.

20:40.258 --> 20:42.454
Look, I know his wife is a smoker.

20:42.561 --> 20:44.893
Just yesterday,
when we saw her at the country club...

20:44.997 --> 20:47.558
she had a cigarette in her hand.

20:48.368 --> 20:49.630
[Snoring]

20:52.606 --> 20:54.700
What, so that's it, Peter?
You're just giving up?

20:54.809 --> 20:56.299
I don't know what else to do, Brian.

20:56.411 --> 20:58.505
I guess we're never
gonna be a family again.

20:58.614 --> 21:00.809
- Hi, Peter.
- Oh, my God, Lois.

21:00.950 --> 21:02.679
- You're all better.
- That's right.

21:02.786 --> 21:05.949
And the doctors say I'll smell like
French fries for the next six months.

21:06.056 --> 21:07.046
I'll enjoy that.

21:07.158 --> 21:09.718
And, Peter, I got a surprise for you.

21:09.827 --> 21:10.953
You got the kids back.

21:11.062 --> 21:14.555
I love you so much,
delicious French-fry wife.

21:14.667 --> 21:18.104
Now we can live with you again
even though you're a dangerous retard.

21:18.204 --> 21:21.606
Don't say "retard," Chris.
We prefer to be called "little people."

21:21.709 --> 21:24.372
Because there's nothing wrong
with being mentally challenged.

21:24.479 --> 21:27.209
In fact, I've learned
that we are superior people.

21:27.316 --> 21:29.615
Above all you dumb brainy smarties.

21:29.719 --> 21:33.087
Someday, you will beg us for mercy
and we will consider it.

21:33.190 --> 21:36.489
Isn't it wonderful
that everything's back to normal?

21:36.594 --> 21:37.562
Yeah.

21:37.729 --> 21:39.356
Oh, God. Nobody move.

21:39.464 --> 21:41.801
- What is it?
- Nothing. Nothing. I'll get it.

21:41.802 --> 22:42.802
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru